cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  Lead-Time-Centric Evaluation of Bearing Anomaly Detectors:
  A Multi-Dataset SCADA Study
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ansh
    family-names: Goyal
    affiliation: "Jaypee Institute of Information Technology, Noida, India"
    email: anshgoyal500@gmail.com
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # add your ORCID, then uncomment
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ansh-Goyal01/Scada-Leadtime-Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible benchmark that makes lead time, gated by a leakage-free
  false-alarm rate, the primary metric for evaluating rolling-element bearing
  anomaly detectors, and uses it to test whether SCADA-rate bin-averaging
  destroys detection lead time. Across four run-to-failure datasets (NASA IMS,
  a real ONGC gas-turbine SCADA record, XJTU-SY, and FEMTO/PRONOSTIA) with
  run-level statistics and Holm correction, the headline finding is
  non-destruction: coarse SCADA-rate logging does not cost bearing-fault warning
  time.
keywords:
  - predictive maintenance
  - prognostics and health management
  - lead time
  - anomaly detection
  - condition monitoring
  - rolling-element bearing
  - SCADA
  - conformal prediction
  - statistical process control
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-06-16"
